{"action": "diagnose", "why": "The evidence is consistent across calls. The ledger consumer is stuck retrying one malformed event forever, and that stalls its whole consumer group.", "diagnosis": {"hypothesis": "Provider event evt_000260 (provider-events partition 1, offset 113) has an invalid amount: 'amount must be positive integer cents'. The webhook-receiver accepted and queued it at about 02:35:33. ledger-consumer had been redeployed at 02:35:31 with BAD_EVENTS=retry. With that setting it retries the same message forever, backing off up to 15s, and never commits past it. While it waits, it stops processing every partition: the posted rate fell to 0 by about 02:36:34. So the ledger group's lag grows on all three partitions as new events arrive (0, then 91, then 305), which fires ConsumerLagHigh. payment-confirmer runs with BAD_EVENTS=dead_letter. It dead-lettered the same message and keeps up. Still open: why the provider sent a non-positive or non-integer amount, and whether the earlier ledger configuration also used retry.", "evidence": [{"call_id": "c1", "shows": "The ledger group's lag was 0 at 02:35:08, 91 at 02:36:08 and 305 at 02:37:08, so the alert is real and the lag is growing."}, {"call_id": "c2", "shows": "ledger-consumer was redeployed at 02:35:31 with LEDGER_HANDLER=idempotent and BAD_EVENTS=retry. payment-confirmer uses BAD_EVENTS=dead_letter."}, {"call_id": "c3", "shows": "ledger-consumer logs 'could not book; will retry the same message' for provider-events/1@113, attempts 3 to 11, error 'amount must be positive integer cents'."}, {"call_id": "c4", "shows": "payment-confirmer dead-lettered the same message, provider-events/1@113, with the same amount error."}, {"call_id": "c5", "shows": "The trace identifies the message as event evt_000260. The receiver queued it with HTTP 200. The ledger span outcome is will_retry 13 or more times over 105s; the confirmer outcome is dead_lettered."}, {"call_id": "c6", "shows": "The lag is spread over all partitions (131, 138, 127), so the whole ledger consumer is blocked, not only partition 1."}, {"call_id": "c7", "shows": "The ledger posted and already_processed rates fell to 0 by 02:36:34. payment-confirmer kept processing at about 3 events/s."}], "confidence": 0.85, "proposed_fix": {"kind": "config_change", "target": "ledger-consumer", "summary": "1. Redeploy ledger-consumer with BAD_EVENTS=dead_letter, as payment-confirmer has. It will then dead-letter evt_000260 and drain the backlog; the idempotent handler makes reprocessing safe. 2. Inspect evt_000260 on the dead-letter queue and in the provider's records. 3. Book or confirm it by hand (data repair) once the correct amount is known. 4. Run money_check afterwards. 5. As a follow-up, consider validating amounts in webhook-receiver."}, "blast_radius": "Only ledger-consumer changes. evt_000260 will be absent from the ledger until it is repaired by hand, so money_check will report it as unposted. Draining about 300 events causes a short burst of load on Postgres. If other malformed events exist, they will also be dead-lettered rather than block the consumer.", "rollback_plan": "Redeploy ledger-consumer with its previous settings (BAD_EVENTS=retry, same image sha256:a145222baa11). Its committed offsets are kept, so nothing is lost. Any dead-lettered events can be replayed from the dead-letter queue once they are fixed."}}
```
